-- title:
--   𝒪[[X₁,…,Xₙ]] over a discrete valuation ring is regular local
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and let $n$ be a natural number. The assertion is that the ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,n)\,\mathcal{O}$ of formal power series in the $n$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ with coefficients in $\mathcal{O}$ satisfies `IsRegularLocalRing`, i.e. it is a Noetherian local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by a number of elements equal to its Krull dimension. Note that $n = 0$ is permitted, in which case the statement reduces to the regularity of $\mathcal{O}$ itself; the dimension of the ring in question is $n+1$, though the numerical value is not part of the conclusion. No further hypothesis on $\mathcal{O}$ (such as completeness, or on the residue field) is imposed, and the variable set is the finite type $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ rather than an arbitrary finite type.
--
--   This is the standard fact that a power series ring in finitely many variables over a discrete valuation ring is regular local, with maximal ideal generated by a uniformiser together with the variables. It supplies the regularity input for the deformation-theoretic arguments in the patching part of the proof, where rings of the form $\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ occur as universal deformation rings and as framing rings, and it is used in the structural analysis of deformation rings of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting.
-- source:
